option to apply Airmoney or code to your order.","Buy with {provider}","Starts processing the payment to complete the order with selected payment method.","Starts processing the payment to complete the order.","Displays amounts of Airmoney that can be applied to your order when selected.","Displays an option to apply a discount or referral code to your purchase when selected.","Applies the selected amount of Airmoney to your order.","Enter a discount or referral code to be applied to your purchase.","Apply the entered code to your purchase.","About unlimited packages","Learn how to earn","Refer friends now","App stores","Footer","Check if you can use Airalo","Directs to relevant section of the page.","Directs to article with list of devices that support eSIMs.","View devices","Displays list of devices for selected brand that support eSIMs.","Opens option to chat to support via WhatsApp.","What is an eSIM","Directs to information about eSIM technology when selected.","Directs to information about device compatibility when selected.","About Airalo section","Huge roaming bills, losing phone service, desperately searching for free WiFi — we didn’t like that stuff, either. That’s why we started Airalo.","A man and woman walking side by side, each looking at their phones.","What is Airalo section","What is Airalo?","Airalo is the world’s first eSIM store. We realized eSIMs — digital SIM cards — can help solve the problem of high roaming bills abroad. Now we offer eSIMs for flexible and affordable coverage in over 200 locations around the world.","A close-up view of a mobile phone showing a screen with various elements and text part of the Airalo mobile app.","Airalo’s mission is to provide global data connectivity for all people. We’re here to liberate you from the roaming limits and fix what’s been broken for years.","A woman is walking with a suitcase in one hand and holding a phone in the other, wearing casual clothing and footwear.","Fast facts section","Fast facts","Year founded","2019","Users","30M+","Countries and regions coverage","200+","Impact section","As a global organization, Airalo has sought to impact and improve the lives of as many people as possible. Including initiatives such as; our Clean Water Initiative in Cameroon, our work with Children International to sponsor children in developing countries, and various relief funds we’ve organized for Ukraine, Myanmar, and Australia.","Learn more about our impact","Directs to Airalo Impact page","A person kneels on the ground, watering a flower with a watering can.","Airalo is an organization that values diversity, inclusion, and equity. As an international organization spanning multiple continents, with various backgrounds and unique experiences, our goal of global connectivity for all is something we live in every day.","Directs to the Our values page.","A collection of colorful puzzle pieces scattered on a black background.","Our team section","Our team","We’re a truly global organization spanning across multiple continents. Our team members all work remotely, but we create opportunities throughout the year to connect with each other in-person.","Illustration of a group of people running while holding cellphones.","Directs to Working at Airalo page","As a global organization, Airalo has invested in many initiatives to promote the health, safety, sustainability, and well-being of others.\u2028\u2028Global equity appears in many forms. At the core of our organization, we believe in bringing global connectivity to everyone on earth. Whatever technology you have and wherever you are, our goal is to have everyone connected. The freedom and liberty to use technology to its full potential have slowly turned from a privilege to a necessity as we become more interconnected.\u2028\u2028As we work towards a digital future, we will continue to promote environmentally-friendly and innovative solutions that reduce the need for plastic and waste from conventional SIM cards.\u2028\u2028Here are the initiatives we’re spearheading:","Relief section","Relief","As a company dedicated to global connectivity, we’re always looking for ways to use our telecom infrastructure and partnerships to bring connectivity where needed. We’ve provided data services for:","The Help Ukraine Connect Fund, 2022","The Airalo team set up the Help Ukraine Connect Fund to support the millions of Ukrainians displaced by war. Funds raised go directly to Ukrainians needing access to data during these difficult times.","The Civil Unrest in Myanmar, 2021","During the civil unrest and conflict in Myanmar, telecom availability was sparse, with most citizens unable to access essential SIM resources. Fortunately, Airalo’s eSIM services were still running. We rapidly became the leading solution for data in the region. Airalo dedicated time, money, and resources to keep Myanmar connected to the rest of the world.","The Australian Wildfires, 2020","The Airalo team mobilized to create a relief fund, with all proceeds of Australian eSIM sales going to those most affected by the tragic natural disaster of Australia’s wildfires.","Education section","Education","Airalo's Children Fund was an initiative born out of collaboration with {helpUrl}, a global non-profit child sponsorship organization.\u2028\u2028The Airalo Fund finances children in developing countries - helping to supply food, water, shelter, and education. Our goal is to sponsor a new child for every employee who joins the company, and by growing Airalo, we hope to build a better future for these children.","Children International","Illustration of books, a graduation cap, eyeglasses, a pencil circling an orange sphere, and a yellow star, representing education and academic achievement.","Clean Water section","Clean Water","Airalo sponsored the rural town of Babou, Cameroon, building a well in the town center. Every day in rural communities throughout Africa, millions of people suffer from the lack of access to clean, safe water. Globally, 1 in 9 people still have no access to clean water, but in many African regions, it's 8 out of 9. Water is a daily and crippling challenge. Without water, you can't grow food, you can't stay healthy, you can't go to school, and you can't keep working. For school-aged children, it's a burden that traps them in poverty. Access to safe water will break the first barrier to a better life and turn problems into potential — unlocking education, economic opportunity, and improved health.","A water tap inside a glass sphere, depicted in a cartoonish style with a colorful design.","Environmental Sustainability section","Environmental Sustainability","Plastic places a tremendous strain on the planet, and we're proud to have built a product that massively reduces the need for plastic SIM cards and their packaging.\u2028\u2028Over 4 billion SIM cards are manufactured each year; that equates to millions of tonnes of plastic being used and discarded, gallons of fuel, and increasingly limited resources utilized in the manufacturing process. As the rest of the world strives to adopt more sustainable manufacturing and distribution practices, Airalo is committed to constantly finding new and innovative ways to reduce our own carbon footprint.","A cartoon illustration of a cellphone with an illuminated screen.","The Airalo team is always growing — and we'd love for you to join us! Browse our job vacancies to find the role that's right for you. Your dream job could be just a scroll away.","A group of girls standing together, wearing colorful clothing and various styles of footwear, depicted in a cartoon style while dancing.","We’re a remote, global team committed to keeping people connected. Sound interesting? Learn more about working at Airalo.","Current opportunities section","Current opportunities","Filter by","Filter department","Opens option to filter job vacancies by department.","Department","Opens option to filter job vacancies by job title.","Job title","Filter j