l don’t connect, toggle Airplane Mode on and off, then wait a moment and try again.","Why is my phone connecting to the wrong network?","In some destinations, your device chooses a network automatically. If your connection is unstable, switch networks manually in your device settings, then reconnect.","Why can’t I find the eSIM on my device?","It may have a label you don’t recognize. Check your SIM list in device settings and rename the eSIM to something easy to spot (for example, “Airalo”), if your device allows it.","Do I need to turn on data roaming?","Sometimes. If you see a step asking you to turn on data roaming, follow it. If you don’t see that step, you can continue with the rest of the connection steps.","Can I use iMessage and FaceTime while using the eSIM?","Yes, on iOS devices — iMessage and FaceTime work over the internet. If you want to keep using your primary number for messaging, you may need to adjust your device settings; carrier charges may apply.","View past eSIMs","My past eSIMs","New Airalo","Directs you to the new Airalo.","Your new Airalo","Joined {date}","Congratulations. You're one of the first to get on board the new Airalo.","See benefits","Benefits","Step {current} of {total}","Add packages as you go.","What is the new Airalo?","The new Airalo lets you set up your device once and stay connected trip after trip. Buy data whenever you need it, across 200+ destinations, without reinstalling or switching eSIMs.","What do I get as a member?","A connection that's ready whenever you travel. You set it up once and it stays with you, so you can land somewhere new and get online straight away. If you run low, you can buy more data on the spot, even with no signal. And you can invite the people you travel with to join you.","Who can join?","Right now it's invite-only, and joining is free (you only pay for data, as you do today). Someone already on the new Airalo saved you a spot. We're opening it up gradually, in waves, so we can keep everything running smoothly as more people come on board. Each new wave gets their own invites to share, which is how it reaches more travelers over time. It isn't available for Airalo for Business accounts yet.","Can I keep using my existing Airalo packages?","Yes. Anything you've already bought keeps working exactly as it is, and the new Airalo simply sits alongside it.","Are all packages and destinations available?","Almost everything you know is here, with a few exceptions for now. The new Airalo is built around data, so calls and text packages aren't part of it yet, and a small number of packages may differ. If you need those, you can switch to the public version anytime.","How many friends can I invite?","You start with a set number of invites to share, and you can always see how many you have left in your profile. Friends who join through you get a few invites of their own to pass on, and so on. The number gets a little smaller at each step, which helps the connection grow steadily rather than all at once. Your invites don't expire, so there's no rush.","Go all abroad with the new Airalo","Invite your friends","I've saved you a spot","{name} wants you to connect easier with Airalo.","{count, plural, one {# friend is in} other {# friends are in}}","You've used {used} of your {total} invites","Your link","Share link","Copy invite link","Invite link copied","Share the link with your friends","Data speed","Full speed for the first 3 GB of data each day (up to 20 Mbps) — after that, lower speed (1 Mbps — enough for messages and maps, but not heavy streaming). Full speed resets every 24 hours, starting from the time you start using your package.","Full speed for the first 3 GB of data each day (up to 20 Mbps) — after that, lower speed (1 Mbps — enough for messages and maps, but not heavy streaming). Full speed resets every 24 hours, starting from the time you start using your package. Data connection stops when your package data runs out.","Full speed until your package data runs out. After that, your data connection stops.","Support chat is unavailable right now. Please try again in a moment.","We couldn't sign you in — continuing as a guest.","Available packages","Select","Switch to the public version to access calls and texts","Switch to use the new Airalo","Switch","You’re using the public version","You can switch back anytime.","You're using the new Airalo","Switch experience?","If you switch, you can access calls and text packages. You won't be able to manage any of your packages purchased while using the new Airalo. \u003Cstrong>You can switch again later.\u003C\u002Fstrong>","Your feedback","Your account is about to Switch. Help us improve by sharing your reason for switching.","I wanted calls and texts","I wanted to share eSIMs with others","I preferred the past version of Airalo","Other","Please add additional details","You have switched from the new Airalo.","Business solutions","Referral reward","I’m buying for someone else","Transfer to someone else","Helping someone stay connected?","\u003Cp>Choose to transfer before you buy — then share via link or QR code, after purchase.\u003C\u002Fp>\n\u003Cp>Once transferred, they can use and manage the package from their Airalo account.\u003C\u002Fp>","Don’t show this again","Available to transfer","How transfer works","You share the package","Send a link or have them scan a QR code from their device.","They receive the package","We’ll transfer the package to their account — they’ll need the Airalo app.","They get connected","Once the package is received, they can get set up and connected in their destination.","Make sure they receive the package on the device they’ll use with Airalo.","Top-up ready","It activates automatically once your current package is used.","Your top-up is used first, then renewals take over automatically.","By completing your purchase, you agree to Airalo's {term} and {privacy}.","terms and conditions","privacy policy","Your friend has invited {count, plural, on